# Copy to `.env` and fill in. NEVER commit the real `.env`.
#
# WARNING — these names carry the `VITE_` prefix, but they are NOT Vite
# variables and the web app does not read them. Vite's root is `frontend/`, and
# `vite.config.ts` sets no `envDir`, so Vite only ever loads `.env*` from
# `frontend/`. This file sits at the repository root and is invisible to it.
#
# Do NOT move this file into `frontend/`. Vite inlines every `VITE_*` variable
# into the client bundle at build time, so `VITE_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY` would be
# published to every browser visitor. That key deploys contracts.

# --- Integration tests / deployer ---
# Private key (0x-prefixed) of a funded StudioNet account. StudioNet is gasless,
# so any account works; this is only needed by `gltest` integration runs.
#
# LEFT EMPTY ON PURPOSE. This file is committed to git, so a real key here would
# be published permanently — git history keeps it even after a later removal,
# and it would reach every clone and remote. Put your own key in the gitignored
# `.env` instead. Everything else in this file is public and is filled in.
#
# Only its PRESENCE and 32-byte hex format are ever checked, by
# tests/direct/test_env_consistency.py. The value is never read or printed.
VITE_DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Contract addresses (the Bradbury two-contract deployment) ---
# ClimateClaim and ClimatePolicy are deployed as SEPARATE contracts, on GenLayer
# Bradbury (chain 4221). Both reached consensus 5/5 AGREE with
# FINISHED_WITH_RETURN; the full record with deploy tx hashes and verification is
# in docs/deployment-bradbury-2026-10-18.md.
#
# The project is split in two because Bradbury enforces a size-dependent gas
# ceiling on deploys: a 793-line contract is rejected with "gas limit too high"
# while 260-line and 427-line contracts are accepted.
#
# Each overrides the matching typed fallback in frontend/src/config/contracts.ts.
# They must stay equal to those fallbacks: test_env_consistency.py fails if they
# diverge.
VITE_CLIMATECLAIM_ADDRESS=0xb80eC5aEa3A62a5F282DB19bA1ccE311b642bC51
VITE_CLIMATEPOLICY_ADDRESS=0xeebb68aEDB14A4184A0C36bAc5528D5f70B8a807

# --- Network chosen for integration runs ---
# Overrides ACTIVE_NETWORK in frontend/src/config/network.ts.
VITE_GLTEST_NETWORK=testnetBradbury

# --- Bradbury RPC endpoint ---
# Must match `rpc_url` / `chain_id` in gltest.integration.config.yaml and the
# typed fallbacks in frontend/src/config/network.ts. tests/direct/
# test_env_consistency.py fails if these three drift apart.
VITE_GENLAYER_RPC_URL=https://rpc-bradbury.genlayer.com
VITE_GENLAYER_CHAIN_ID=4221

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Frontend (frontend/) — nothing to configure here, and deliberately so.
#
# The app reads its network, contract address and explorer URL from typed
# config files, not from environment variables:
#
#   frontend/src/config/network.ts    chains, RPC URLs, explorer availability
#   frontend/src/config/contracts.ts  contract address and schema-derived method names
#
# This is on purpose. Moving the contract address into an inlined `VITE_*`
# variable buys nothing and creates a second place for it to drift out of sync
# with the deployed contract.
#
# There are NO secrets in the app. It is read-only by default; sending a
# transaction requires a browser wallet, which holds its own key and is never
# given to this codebase.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------